            "code": 4,
            "input": 1,
            "field": "next"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "s4-in0",
          "prompt": "In non-overlapping mode, determine next state from S4 (match state) when input IN = 0.",
          "kind": "seq-state-table-cell",
          "expected": {
            "kind": "state-table-row",
            "nextState": "0"
          },
          "context": {
            "spec": {
              "kind": "detector",
              "pattern": "1011",
              "machine": "moore",
              "overlapping": false,
              "flipFlop": "D"
            },
            "code": 4,
            "input": 0,
            "field": "next"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "s4-out",
          "prompt": "Determine Moore output Z associated with state S4.",
          "kind": "seq-state-table-cell",
          "expected": {
            "kind": "state-table-row",
            "output": "1"
          },
          "context": {
            "spec": {
              "kind": "detector",
              "pattern": "1011",
              "machine": "moore",
              "overlapping": false,
              "flipFlop": "D"
            },
            "code": 4,
            "input": 0,
            "field": "output"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "eq-z-moore",
          "prompt": "Derive the minimal Boolean equation for Moore output Z.",
          "kind": "seq-equation",
          "expected": {
            "kind": "boolean-step",
            "resultingExpression": "Q2"
          },
          "context": {
            "spec": {
              "kind": "detector",
              "pattern": "1011",
              "machine": "moore",
              "overlapping": false,
              "flipFlop": "D"
            },
            "functionName": "Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "eq-d2",
          "prompt": "Derive the minimal Boolean excitation equation for flip-flop input D2.",
          "kind": "seq-equation",
          "expected": {
            "kind": "boolean-step",
            "resultingExpression": "Q1 & Q0 & IN"
          },
          "context": {
            "spec": {
              "kind": "detector",
              "pattern": "1011",
              "machine": "moore",
              "overlapping": false,
              "flipFlop": "D"
            },
            "functionName": "D2"
          }
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": {
        "D2": "Q1 & Q0 & IN",
        "Z": "Q2"
      },
      "explanation": [
        "In state S3 ('101' matched), receiving IN = 1 completes the sequence '1011', transitioning to state S4.",
        "Because detection is non-overlapping, none of the bits from '1011' can be reused. However, the new incoming input 1 could be the start of a new sequence, so the machine transitions to state S1.",
        "If the incoming input from S4 is 0, no prefix is matched, so the machine resets completely to S0.",
        "In a Moore machine, output depends strictly on current state; state S4 represents full recognition, so Z = 1.",
        "Using 3 state bits for 5 states, S4 is encoded as 100 (Q2=1). With unused states 5..7 as don't-cares, output Z minimizes to Z = Q2.",
        "Bit Q2 turns on only when entering S4 from S3 (011) with IN = 1, giving D2 = Q1 & Q0 & IN."
      ],
      "learningObjective": "Synthesize a 5-state Moore sequence detector with non-overlapping recognition and evaluate state decoding logic.",
